{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/519213-demon-the-fallen-in-nomine-awesome","id":519213,"title":"Demon the Fallen + In Nomine = Awesome?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-19T03:13:59-07:00","id":519213,"title":"Demon the Fallen + In Nomine = Awesome?","content":"I'm sure it's come up before, but if someone could just point me in the direction, I'll check out what I'm sure is a tired topic in the CWoD forums! If it hasn't come up though:<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of just changing the names of the Lores to Songs, using In Nomine setting, but Fallen rules. For the most part, they look pretty easy to convert back and forth. The most time consuming part would be the Songs, but, like I said, it's simple just to change a name. If I remember right, they can both &quot;feel&quot; powers being used. Pacts and Faith are a welcome addition as is the Form. I think it would work very well. I don't think I'd convert EVERYTHING though. There's no reason to convert EVERY band of demon to it's Prince if no one is going to use it, same goes for the ranks.<br /> <br /> Anyway, like I said, if there's a thread already up, point me at it. If you have any ideas or experience with this thought, that would be welcome as well. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1101-blindst","name":"blindST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T13:50:21-07:00","id":525869,"title":"","content":"Would be interesting to see this. Back before Demon the Fallen was conceived, I had a fallen angel PC that a friend ran in one of my Vampire Chronicles. We used In Nomine as a basis and incorporated a lot of elements of The Prophecy franchise as well. That game had ended by the time D:tF came out, but I would have loved to have converted his character to Demon rules.<br /> <br /> The weakest part of D:tF was always the setting. I love the feel of the game, the Houses were fantastic, the Lores excellent... but the setting just falls flat. One thing I didn't like was the Byronic anti-hero overtones they pushed. It's like someone misread Milton and bought what the Devil in Paradise Lost was selling.<br /> <br /> The major reason I was dissatisfied with the setting, though was the cop-out on the matter of Hell. Apparently, Hell is nothing. Hell is void. Hell is <i>boring.</i> Hell is a bunch of demons huddled in a dark room throwing a hissy fit because they lost. They form little cliques and basically just argue for eternity about what happened to Lucifer. It's hip, and edgy, and dull. Suddenly, Hell isn't even a place for mortal souls.<br /> <br /> The setting of In Nomine is much more vibrant, although admittedly I prefer Angelic forces to be more in the background.<br /> <br /> There was another roleplaying game that came out a little while ago called The Seventh Seal. It's way heavy on the Christian apocalyptic overtones (so heavy in fact that the setting doesn't work if unless Christianity is the ultimate truth of the universe - other religions were, at best, considered &quot;misunderstandings&quot; of Christian truths, which lessened the game considerably in my view), but it's system and setup were essentially lifted right out of White Wolf - it would be simple to drop it directly into Demon the Fallen. Definitely give it a look for ideas on how the mortal servants of Angelic forces might operate. They would work well as proto-Imbued: ancient orders dating back to the first time the Messengers intervened.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5525-rebelwithoutaclan","name":"RebelWithoutAClan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5525_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T18:03:25-07:00","id":526141,"title":"","content":"Slightly tangential to this, I've always wanted to do a hybrid of <b>In Nomine</b> and <b>Scion</b>. My first instinct was to use <b>Scion</b>'s Pantheons to flesh out <b>In Nomine</b>'s Ethereal Realm; though that ran into the problem of casting the gods of the non-Abrahamic religions as little more than ascended figments of human imagination. My second take on the idea was to constrain the Ethereal Realm to the Veil of Dreams and to port the \u201cpagan gods\u201d into the Celestial Realm, which in this version more closely resembled <b>Scion</b>'s Overworld and Underworld (with Heaven and Hell \u201cmerely\u201d being the Abrahamic Overworld and Underworld). Mechanically, I leaned more toward <b>In Nomine</b> than toward <b>Scion</b>, as I considered the former to be the least broken of the two. At this point, though, I'm waiting to see what the second edition of <b>Scion</b> comes up with before I attemp anything. Who knows? Maybe it will provide a setting that includes [b]In Nomine[/i]-like elements built-in. <br /> <br /> I have other thoughts that are more relevant to the original post; I'll get to them later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T19:22:09-07:00","id":526221,"title":"","content":"<u>From <b>In Nomine</b></u><br /> \u2022 The War, with each side thinking that it holds the moral high ground and the truth being left entirely up to the Storyteller. <br /> \u2022 Angels and Demons both being playable character types, feeling distinct from each other but being more similar than either would ever care to admit. <br /> \u2022 Falling and Redemption. To the extent that there <i>are</i> differences, it's possible to switch from one to the other. <br /> \u2022 Celestial Form. When an angel or demon is exposed for what it is, no longer clothed by flesh, it should be a spirit-like entity. <br /> <br /> <u>From <b>Demon: the Fallen</b></u><br /> \u2022 the seven Houses. The angels will need different nicknames.<br /> \u2022 Torment. Angels should have an analogous trait, representing how out-of-sync with the Heavenly Host they are. <br /> <br /> <u>From <b>Demon: the Descent</b></u><br /> \u2022 Cover. Conceptually, this merges the notions of Vessel and Role found in <b>In Nomine</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div ali