ave converted his character to Demon rules.<br /> <br /> The weakest part of D:tF was always the setting. I love the feel of the game, the Houses were fantastic, the Lores excellent... but the setting just falls flat. One thing I didn't like was the Byronic anti-hero overtones they pushed. It's like someone misread Milton and bought what the Devil in Paradise Lost was selling.<br /> <br /> The major reason I was dissatisfied with the setting, though was the cop-out on the matter of Hell. Apparently, Hell is nothing. Hell is void. Hell is <i>boring.</i> Hell is a bunch of demons huddled in a dark room throwing a hissy fit because they lost. They form little cliques and basically just argue for eternity about what happened to Lucifer. It's hip, and edgy, and dull. Suddenly, Hell isn't even a place for mortal souls.<br /> <br /> The setting of In Nomine is much more vibrant, although admittedly I prefer Angelic forces to be more in the background.<br /> <br /> There was another roleplaying game that came out a little while ago called The Seventh Seal. It's way heavy on the Christian apocalyptic overtones (so heavy in fact that the setting doesn't work if unless Christianity is the ultimate truth of the universe - other religions were, at best, considered &quot;misunderstandings&quot; of Christian truths, which lessened the game considerably in my view), but it's system and setup were essentially lifted right out of White Wolf - it would be simple to drop it directly into Demon the Fallen. Definitely give it a look for ideas on how the mortal servants of Angelic forces might operate. They would work well as proto-Imbued: ancient orders dating back to the first time the Messengers intervened.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's some good advice here, Thanx ...<br /> <br /> I too had issue with Demon the Fallen, however, more so do to the misconception of the word &quot;demon&quot; being &quot;Fallen Angel&quot;. When the origins of the word Literally translates to &quot;Disembodied Spirit&quot; (or Spirits of the dead Giants from BCE).<br /> <br /> I never looked through a Seventh Seal book before, so I'm gonna give one a glance over.<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6040-quiet-storm","name":"Quiet Storm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T11:01:38-07:00","id":528981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quiet Storm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/519213-demon-the-fallen-in-nomine-awesome?p=527389#post527389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's some good advice here, Thanx ...<br /> <br /> I too had issue with Demon the Fallen, however, more so do to the misconception of the word &quot;demon&quot; being &quot;Fallen Angel&quot;. When the origins of the word Literally translates to &quot;Disembodied Spirit&quot; (or Spirits of the dead Giants from BCE).<br /> <br /> I never looked through a Seventh Seal book before, so I'm gonna give one a glance over.<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Daemons are merely forces , good or evil.<br /> Many genius locii are considered daemons in the classical sense","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T20:59:17-07:00","id":530620,"title":"","content":"I always liked the idea of using the in nomine version of the genesis story, in which evolution was the origin of humanity and Eden was an experiment meant to test humanity's morals as a means of smoothing over the evolution vs creationism battle between WtA and VtM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{